  "cards": [
    {"dot": "emerald", "title": "Out: from a tap to the backends", "items": [
      "A single input tile sends data under its own id, steps under each step's id, a toggle the value it asks for; the profile's fixed data comes along (core.py 123–134).",
      "parse() keeps known fields only: a part is a scalar, {jpeg, w, h, text} or {code, format}; at most 12 parts and 2 photos of 1400 KB base64 (protocol.py 105–156).",
      "emit() numbers the event, keeps it for the setup page (photos of the last 6, in memory), and hands it to every adapter; one that fails misses it, the others go on (core.py 69–86)."]},
    {"dot": "cyan", "title": "In: from a backend to the phone", "items": [
      "Each adapter passes the raw text to command(); a refused command comes back as an error event to that adapter alone (core.py 155–191).",
      "state is kept with its label, so a phone that comes back gets it in its profile message (core.py 148–152, 173–182). toast, say, ask, vibrate, open and home need a phone: without one, error \"no phone\"."]},
    {"dot": "rose", "title": "Held back", "items": [
      "The setup page's log replaces each photo by its size; the photo itself is at /api/photo, this PC only (protocol.py 252–259, wsserver.py 341–356).",
      "edge-in can hand the photos on as base64, as Buffers or drop them (edge-in.js 9–19)."]}
  ]
